WEBVTT

00:03.215 --> 00:05.302
[wind whistling]

00:09.310 --> 00:12.107
[seagull cawing]

00:14.863 --> 00:16.909
[footsteps approaching]

00:20.040 --> 00:22.419
You still haven't told me
your reasoning yet.

00:22.921 --> 00:25.969
Here we are searching for Geass fragments.

00:26.052 --> 00:29.559
So why did you give that girl your Geass?

00:30.603 --> 00:32.022
Just for your amusement?

00:32.398 --> 00:35.738
Or because she's related to Kaguya?

00:36.447 --> 00:37.617
Who knows?

00:37.701 --> 00:38.869
[chuckles softly]

00:39.663 --> 00:43.169
But you're not planning on involving
yourself any further, are you?

00:45.800 --> 00:50.142
We are beings who exist
outside the conventions of this world.

00:53.023 --> 00:54.358
[C.C.] True.

01:01.080 --> 01:03.084
[♪ opening theme song playing]

02:33.682 --> 02:37.189
[reporter] <i>Princess Sherry me Britannia,
mother of Empress Sakuya,</i>

02:37.649 --> 02:41.447
<i>was the eldest child
of the 98th Emperor Charles.</i>

02:42.032 --> 02:46.750
<i>However, before Emperor Charles
ascended the throne, she married,</i>

02:46.833 --> 02:49.255
<i>thereby forfeiting her claim
to succession.</i>

02:49.338 --> 02:50.550
BLACK KNIGHTS HACHINOHE BASE

02:50.633 --> 02:52.595
<i>However, it is evident that Empress Sakuya</i>

02:52.679 --> 02:54.849
<i>is of legitimate imperial lineage--</i>

02:56.269 --> 02:57.271
<i>We've been outplayed.</i>

02:57.981 --> 03:00.235
<i>If Sakuya Sumeragi ascends to the throne,</i>

03:00.318 --> 03:03.993
<i>given her blood ties to Kaguya and us,
the United Federation of Nations</i>

03:04.076 --> 03:05.663
<i>will act even more cautiously.</i>

03:06.497 --> 03:09.546
<i>The third liberation operation
will likely be further delayed.</i>

03:10.422 --> 03:11.925
General Commander Cornelia...

03:12.927 --> 03:15.725
It's been three months
since I returned to the Black Knights,

03:15.808 --> 03:17.979
but I'm still not used to
being called that.

03:18.897 --> 03:20.568
It frustrates me.

03:21.319 --> 03:24.366
During the first and second liberations,

03:24.450 --> 03:27.205
if you and Lieutenant Colonel Tohdoh
had been there,

03:27.289 --> 03:29.376
we would not have been defeated
so easily...

03:29.460 --> 03:31.172
<i>You overestimate me.</i>

03:31.255 --> 03:33.510
<i>The Situmpe Wall is strong,</i>

03:33.594 --> 03:36.432
<i>and Norland von Lunebelg
is a formidable foe.</i>

03:36.516 --> 03:40.983
<i>Above all, they have the Damocles
mounted with F.L.E.I.J.A.</i>

03:41.693 --> 03:44.073
[Cornelia] <i>These are not opponents
we can easily defeat...</i>

03:45.993 --> 03:49.249
<i>Of course, we have no intention
of losing either.</i>

03:49.751 --> 03:54.176
<i>Just to confirm, the girl
who is now empress is, in fact, a decoy?</i>

03:54.552 --> 03:55.554
Correct.

03:55.638 --> 03:58.142
Princess Sakuya has concealed her identity

03:58.226 --> 04:01.232
and is currently collaborating
with Kuroto's organization.

04:01.608 --> 04:03.111
<i>That should work to our advantage.</i>

04:03.194 --> 04:04.698
<i>I have approved the budget.</i>

04:04.781 --> 04:07.662
<i>Prepare the second convoy
of transport ships.</i>

04:08.371 --> 04:09.373
[Shiro] Understood!

04:11.670 --> 04:13.464
Sherry's daughter, huh?

04:14.425 --> 04:17.097
Only a niece of mine could be so reckless.

04:17.431 --> 04:20.103
NEO-BRITANNIA GOVERNMENT OFFICE
FRONT SHRINE

04:23.192 --> 04:25.906
[man] Hard to believe that
they made <i>her</i> our empress overnight...

04:25.990 --> 04:28.453
[man 2] I hear she's half Eleven.

04:28.537 --> 04:29.748
What on earth is going on?

04:29.831 --> 04:33.463
[woman] But it seems the real power
remains with Lord Norland.

04:33.547 --> 04:35.968
[man 2] I see. Well, that's a relief.

04:37.220 --> 04:41.353
[Sakura] <i>I wasn't wrong, was I, Sa-chan?</i>

04:42.732 --> 04:44.736
[Rozé] <i>By becoming empress,</i>

04:44.819 --> 04:47.909
she may have some power
to implement policies for the Japanese.

04:47.992 --> 04:48.994
SEVEN SHINING STARS HAKODATE HIDEOUT

04:50.121 --> 04:53.587
She might be able to alter the course
of Neo-Britannia, ever so slightly.

04:54.129 --> 04:57.344
She believes the real Sakuya Sumeragi
would think this way.

04:57.427 --> 05:00.350
That's why Sakura accepted
the role of empress.

05:00.935 --> 05:04.776
Though, more accurately,
it was Norland who made her do it.

05:04.859 --> 05:06.780
But that strategy...

05:06.905 --> 05:09.451
Yes, it's unlikely to succeed...

05:09.953 --> 05:14.461
We're talking about someone who returns
diplomatic delegations as corpses.

05:14.546 --> 05:17.510
Attempting to change things
from the inside will take too much time.

05:18.010 --> 05:20.641
[Rozé] How many lives would be sacrificed
in the meantime?

05:22.310 --> 05:23.522
We'll fight.

05:23.605 --> 05:25.734
We'll fight and take it all back.

05:26.235 --> 05:29.283
This land... and Sakura as well.

05:30.076 --> 05:31.120
[Kuroto] Indeed.

05:31.705 --> 05:33.291
[Oda] Say that again!

05:34.459 --> 05:37.592
[Wakui] We've no idea where
Princess Sakuya has been all this time,

05:37.675 --> 05:39.679
only for her to appear
out of nowhere as empress.

05:40.180 --> 05:42.685
[Wakui] You sure she hasn't sided
with the Britannians?

05:42.768 --> 05:44.564
Of all the unfounded accusations!

05:44.981 --> 05:48.154
I mean, she's half Britannian as well.

05:48.237 --> 05:50.743
It's not like we've all forgotten that.

05:50.826 --> 05:54.751
During the Far East Incident,
Governor Jugo tirelessly negotiated

05:54.834 --> 05:56.588
to ensure this area suffered no harm.

05:56.671 --> 06:00.303
[Yasunaga] And when Britannia took
control, Princess Sherry quickly moved

06:00.386 --> 06:03.518
to protect the Japanese by creating
the Special Administrative District.

06:03.602 --> 06:05.648
-All the more reason--
-[Wakui] I'm worried!

06:05.731 --> 06:07.610
Can we avoid conflict?

06:07.693 --> 06:10.991
Or will we have to fight Empress Sakuya?

06:12.787 --> 06:15.834
[Yasunaga] Tell me... C'mon.

06:18.089 --> 06:20.511
SCISSORMAN DOMAIN, ASAHIKAWA

06:20.594 --> 06:22.556
-[device trilling, crackling]
-I'm telling the truth!

06:22.640 --> 06:23.767
I don't remember anything!

06:24.393 --> 06:27.566
<i>When I came around,
the cell door was unlocked!</i>

06:28.234 --> 06:30.071
<i>I'm just as clueless
as to what happened...</i>

06:30.154 --> 06:35.958
But the surveillance camera footage
clearly shows you unlocking it.

06:36.041 --> 06:40.008
<i>Please, believe me!
I haven't done anything!</i>

06:40.091 --> 06:41.886
[grunting in pain]

06:44.517 --> 06:47.147
[staff] Sir Christoph, it's nearly time.

06:47.230 --> 06:49.944
Oh, it's fine. Leave me.

06:50.028 --> 06:51.030
[staff] But...

06:51.573 --> 06:53.702
Let the Divock boy hunt down the remnants.

06:53.702 --> 06:55.622
Let the Divock boy hunt down the remnants.
He seems quite eager, anyhow.

06:55.622 --> 06:56.248
He seems quite eager, anyhow.

07:00.298 --> 07:02.511
-[all panting]
-[rumbling]

07:09.274 --> 07:10.401
[men grunt]

07:10.485 --> 07:12.948
Damn you, Neo-Britannia!

07:13.032 --> 07:14.034
Sir, are you all right?!

07:14.117 --> 07:15.119
I'm fine.

07:15.203 --> 07:17.082
Let's head straight
to the rendezvous point!

07:17.165 --> 07:18.167
Let's go!

07:26.726 --> 07:28.647
-[people clamoring]
-This way, sir!

07:30.859 --> 07:34.867
Are you hell-bent on completely
crushing the seeds of our resistance?

07:39.752 --> 07:42.716
Hurry, now. Run along.

07:43.050 --> 07:47.142
Or else I might actually
end up killing you!

07:54.991 --> 07:56.828
[Rozé] How're things over there?

07:57.245 --> 07:58.957
[Natalia] <i>We're fine.</i>

07:59.040 --> 08:00.418
<i>Everything's calm here.</i>

08:00.711 --> 08:03.508
But the government is in shambles.

08:03.925 --> 08:06.848
A handful of individuals
from the military faction

08:06.931 --> 08:09.019
withheld the information
until the last minute,

08:09.102 --> 08:11.398
<i>so now we're scrambling
to do damage control.</i>

08:11.481 --> 08:12.776
Lucky you.

08:13.402 --> 08:14.864
<i>What about on your end?</i>

08:15.448 --> 08:17.410
Yeah, we're fine.

08:17.493 --> 08:20.082
<i>Although things are a bit chaotic.</i>

08:20.166 --> 08:21.628
That's not what I mean...

08:22.003 --> 08:23.548
<i>-I mean you specifically.</i>
-[gasps softly]

08:28.057 --> 08:30.186
I'm fine, yeah.

08:30.896 --> 08:32.106
Talk to you later then.

08:32.190 --> 08:33.818
-[device beeps]
-[meows]

08:35.822 --> 08:36.908
[knock on door]

08:38.202 --> 08:39.997
Rozé, it's time.

08:40.498 --> 08:42.043
The meeting is starting.

08:42.126 --> 08:43.128
On my way.

08:47.554 --> 08:48.557
I think...

08:49.099 --> 08:50.519
I'm in love.

08:52.188 --> 08:53.566
[Sakuya] <i>Oh, jeez...</i>

08:55.988 --> 08:57.365
We've received a report.

08:58.075 --> 09:00.622
It appears the North Wolf Army
and the Eastern Dawn Brigade

09:00.706 --> 09:02.960
were attacked by Neo-Britannia.

09:03.586 --> 09:06.634
Commander Iwamoto and Tomi
managed to escape,

09:06.718 --> 09:08.722
but their remaining forces
were greatly reduced.

09:09.222 --> 09:12.353
We're going up against the
Neo-Britannia Army in our current state?

09:12.437 --> 09:13.815
And against Empress Sakuya?

09:14.149 --> 09:16.320
One thing from me on that.

09:17.698 --> 09:20.537
We've learned that Sakuya Sumeragi
was held prisoner

09:20.621 --> 09:22.791
in Abashiri Concentration Camp
until recently.

09:22.875 --> 09:24.294
[all gasp]

09:26.674 --> 09:28.469
During our mission
to rescue General Kuroto,

09:28.553 --> 09:30.222
the Weiss Queen showed up, right?

09:30.932 --> 09:32.686
I was curious, so I did some research.

09:33.187 --> 09:35.066
No public records.

09:35.149 --> 09:38.531
But found in the Apollo's battle data...

09:39.240 --> 09:40.242
was this.

09:40.326 --> 09:41.328
[people gasp]

09:42.080 --> 09:44.334
I'm glad we at least managed
to uncover this.

09:44.417 --> 09:45.378
[Yoko] What does this mean?

09:45.962 --> 09:49.094
Sakuya Sumeragi, confined in Abashiri,

09:49.177 --> 09:52.266
was transferred to the government office
for unknown reasons.

09:52.350 --> 09:55.732
There are also rumors that
the late Emperor Callis was assassinated.

09:56.818 --> 09:59.740
[Rozé] <i>His official cause of death
is heart failure,</i>

09:59.824 --> 10:01.536
<i>but whether or not that's true...</i>

10:02.286 --> 10:05.669
It's well-known
that Callis was Norland's puppet.

10:06.128 --> 10:08.925
So all that's changed
is the puppet's name.

10:09.342 --> 10:13.267
[Rozé] In short, it's reasonable to assume
that Sakuya Sumeragi

10:13.350 --> 10:14.979
is being manipulated by Norland.

10:15.689 --> 10:16.941
Make no mistake.

10:17.024 --> 10:19.112
Our enemy is not Sakuya Sumeragi.

10:19.613 --> 10:22.661
It's Norland
and the Neo-Britannia Army he leads.

10:23.036 --> 10:25.584
Yeah! That's right! Exactly!

10:25.667 --> 10:28.255
The enemy is Norland and Neo-Britannia!

10:28.338 --> 10:30.384
Hearing that clears things up for me.

10:30.468 --> 10:31.679
Me too!

10:32.681 --> 10:34.935
[all clamor in agreement]

10:35.019 --> 10:37.858
While you're all fired up,
I have some good news to share.

10:38.860 --> 10:41.198
The second convoy
of transport ships is on its way.

10:41.281 --> 10:43.620
[all exclaim]

10:43.703 --> 10:46.416
NEO-BRITANNIA GOVERNMENT OFFICE
IMPERIAL PALACE

11:17.436 --> 11:19.942
I failed to keep my promise
to the emperor.

11:21.111 --> 11:25.286
It's hard to accept.
The emperor was only 10 years old.

11:30.337 --> 11:32.300
[Kosaka] Hey, over here!

11:32.843 --> 11:34.178
[Hinagata] Hurry up.

11:34.262 --> 11:35.807
The ships are nearly here.

11:36.517 --> 11:38.813
Wait, where's Haruka?

11:39.314 --> 11:42.069
Didn't show up. Apparently,
she's off doing target practice.

11:42.988 --> 11:46.996
<i>Said she wants to improve her
weak shooting skills to contribute more.</i>

11:47.455 --> 11:49.083
But there are a lot of ways

11:49.167 --> 11:51.212
she can contribute besides fighting.

11:51.296 --> 11:53.676
[gasps] You're actually sounding sensible
for once!

11:53.760 --> 11:55.095
Wait, that girl!

11:55.179 --> 11:58.978
What if she's practicing
because she wants to pilot the ace unit?!

11:59.605 --> 12:02.986
[Oda] <i>I mean, that Knightmare
really was awesome!</i>

12:03.445 --> 12:06.368
[exclaims] Man, do I wanna pilot it!

12:06.451 --> 12:08.873
I see... Well, good luck.

12:09.541 --> 12:12.839
But honestly,
I'd like General Kuroto to ride it.

12:13.423 --> 12:15.804
[Oda] During his time
in the Japan Liberation Front,

12:15.887 --> 12:18.392
his military record was just incredible!

12:19.143 --> 12:23.110
Especially his spear handling.
They say no one could match him!

12:23.193 --> 12:26.199
Hey! You lot! The boat is arriving.

12:26.617 --> 12:28.453
Arriving... where?

12:28.538 --> 12:30.457
-[water gurgling]
-[all] Huh?

12:33.840 --> 12:35.009
What the heck is that!

12:35.092 --> 12:36.469
A... submarine?

12:37.054 --> 12:40.185
[Rozé] It's a large-scale submarine
modified for transport.

12:41.146 --> 12:43.901
Let's hurry up and move the cargo
or it'll cause a backlog.

12:52.544 --> 12:56.844
Second-Lieutenant Minato Sakai,
from the Black Knights' Hachinohe Base,

12:57.344 --> 13:00.017
accompanying the transport ship as escort.

13:02.313 --> 13:03.315
I am also here

13:04.066 --> 13:05.820
as the escort of this individual.

13:06.530 --> 13:09.912
Pleasure to meet you.
My name is Nina Einstein.

13:17.468 --> 13:20.474
This is the latest model
developed by our research lab.

13:21.101 --> 13:23.523
The F.L.E.I.J.A. Eliminator.

13:24.566 --> 13:27.321
[Nina] With the initial model,
in the 19 seconds prior to detonation,

13:27.404 --> 13:30.829
environmental data had to be
input manually into the program.

13:30.912 --> 13:34.126
Even then, its window of efficacy
was only 0.04 seconds.

13:34.418 --> 13:37.717
It was also necessary
to hit the F.L.E.I.J.A. directly,

13:37.801 --> 13:39.596
which was a very restrictive condition.

13:40.264 --> 13:41.474
However, with this new model,

13:41.559 --> 13:44.480
if the first switch is activated
when it is launched,

13:44.565 --> 13:46.861
the environmental data
is input automatically.

13:46.944 --> 13:50.158
If it is within 100 meters
of the F.L.E.I.J.A. when it detonates,

13:50.242 --> 13:51.954
it will neutralize the explosion.

13:53.290 --> 13:56.212
We've managed to simplify
the conditions to this extent...

13:56.797 --> 13:58.425
That's simplified?

13:58.509 --> 14:01.222
I mean, the F.L.E.I.J.A. flies
at lightning speed, right?

14:01.306 --> 14:03.978
Trying to get within 100 meters of it...

14:04.061 --> 14:06.482
[Oda] That's gonna be one heck of a job.

14:06.567 --> 14:07.819
Well...

14:08.445 --> 14:09.907
Can you do it, Ash?

14:09.990 --> 14:11.159
It's not impossible.

14:11.827 --> 14:14.833
If we can predict its trajectory
and identify its target location,

14:14.917 --> 14:16.419
it would increase our odds.

14:16.921 --> 14:19.551
It's a significant improvement
over 0.04 seconds.

14:19.843 --> 14:22.306
Easy for you to say...

14:22.389 --> 14:25.103
I was the one who created the F.L.E.I.J.A.

14:25.813 --> 14:29.863
At the time, I was so caught up
in my calculations being validated

14:30.364 --> 14:34.080
[voice breaking] that I didn't stop to
consider the potential consequences.

14:34.873 --> 14:38.673
As a result,
I caused the deaths of millions...

14:39.591 --> 14:41.469
I want to stop the F.L.E.I.J.A.!

14:42.096 --> 14:43.849
[Nina] Please, help me do this...

14:45.060 --> 14:46.062
[door opens]

14:47.106 --> 14:50.028
[Rozé] Here's your room, Dr. Einstein.

14:50.780 --> 14:52.701
You'll be staying with Sakai.

14:52.784 --> 14:55.623
We're short on rooms. Sorry about that.

14:55.707 --> 14:56.709
No problem.

14:57.752 --> 15:00.007
-That was impressive just now.
-Huh?

15:00.382 --> 15:03.430
Everyone seemed moved by what you said.

15:03.514 --> 15:05.977
Although there might be some
who have mixed feelings.

15:06.687 --> 15:08.983
You're a Britannian, right?

15:09.568 --> 15:11.780
Why are you helping the resistance?

15:12.657 --> 15:14.870
You're one to talk, doc.

15:14.953 --> 15:17.751
You took the risk of
coming to Hokkaido, after all.

15:18.251 --> 15:19.755
But to answer your question...

15:20.338 --> 15:24.180
It's a cliché, but maybe it's because
I have something to protect.

15:24.263 --> 15:25.432
[knock on door]

15:26.977 --> 15:28.354
Excuse me, Doctor.

15:29.065 --> 15:30.067
Rozé.

15:30.150 --> 15:31.194
Got it.

15:31.277 --> 15:33.198
[Rozé] Doc, please stay in your room.

15:33.281 --> 15:34.743
We don't want to fan the flames.

15:34.826 --> 15:35.828
All right.

15:35.912 --> 15:38.709
-Second-Lieutenant, please look after her.
-[Sakai] Understood.

15:40.963 --> 15:42.257
[all] Huh?

15:42.341 --> 15:43.803
So, you finally showed up.

15:43.886 --> 15:46.057
Apologies for keeping you waiting.

15:46.390 --> 15:48.771
[Iwamoto] It's been a long time, Kuroto.

15:48.854 --> 15:51.067
Likewise, Commander Iwamoto.

15:51.610 --> 15:54.991
We know why you've gathered us here.

15:55.075 --> 15:59.375
You're plotting to bring
the decimated North Wolf Army

15:59.458 --> 16:02.297
and Eastern Dawn Brigade
under your control, aren't you?

16:02.715 --> 16:04.093
Hardly.

16:04.426 --> 16:06.598
The organizations opposing Britannia

16:06.682 --> 16:09.980
are in a crisis of survival
due to the enemy's repeated attacks.

16:10.355 --> 16:14.614
I believe now is the time
for us to unite and work together.

16:14.698 --> 16:16.450
You're all talk!

16:16.952 --> 16:18.831
If you are ready to cooperate,

16:19.456 --> 16:23.924
we will provide you
with these Knightmares and ammunition.

16:24.718 --> 16:26.930
[men exclaim, clamor]

16:29.351 --> 16:31.648
[Iwamoto] Where did you acquire all this?

16:31.982 --> 16:33.861
From the Black Knights.

16:34.361 --> 16:36.992
Using our own personal channel.

16:37.535 --> 16:38.579
Thought as much.

16:39.079 --> 16:42.211
You're bribing us for our allegiance.

16:42.294 --> 16:43.254
[Kuroto] No.

16:43.338 --> 16:48.431
Even if that's not your intent,
if we feel indebted to you, it's the same!

16:48.807 --> 16:50.895
Well then, what would you like us to do?

16:50.978 --> 16:53.567
I spoke with Commander Tomi.

16:53.651 --> 16:58.159
The three of us will form a council
to plan and conduct operations.

16:58.661 --> 16:59.829
A council?

16:59.913 --> 17:02.334
That will compromise
our ability to act swiftly.

17:02.417 --> 17:04.046
We're well aware of that.

17:04.129 --> 17:07.804
If you can't accept these terms,
then cooperation is off the table.

17:09.181 --> 17:13.314
I guess uniting the three factions
is a pipe dream after all.

17:13.398 --> 17:14.526
Perhaps...

17:14.609 --> 17:16.362
[Rozé sighs]

17:16.989 --> 17:19.285
And you call yourselves adults?

17:19.953 --> 17:21.790
All I see is a bunch of idiots.

17:23.042 --> 17:25.463
Hey! Watch your mouth, kid!

17:25.548 --> 17:29.388
For starters, your reliance on this
Britannian doesn't sit right with me!

17:29.471 --> 17:32.645
Have you forgotten your pride
and honor as a Japanese?

17:33.271 --> 17:35.358
That's besides the point.

17:35.442 --> 17:36.820
Let me ask you this instead.

17:36.903 --> 17:38.991
Why did you guys come here today?

17:39.491 --> 17:41.538
You know yourselves, don't you?

17:41.622 --> 17:45.003
That there's no future for you
if things go on like this.

17:46.548 --> 17:50.013
That said, I can understand
where you're coming from.

17:50.514 --> 17:51.516
So...

17:52.142 --> 17:54.396
how about an alliance?

17:54.939 --> 17:56.526
An alliance?

17:56.860 --> 18:00.200
[Rozé] That's right.
All of us here share one common goal.

18:00.283 --> 18:03.081
To reclaim Japan from Neo-Britannia.

18:03.164 --> 18:05.460
So to that end,
we work together as an allied force.

18:05.920 --> 18:08.424
Since not having a unified
command structure is a bad idea,

18:08.509 --> 18:10.846
I'd like to ask General Kuroto
to take overall command.

18:11.347 --> 18:14.729
But for actual combat, Commander Iwamoto
will command the North Wolf Army

18:14.813 --> 18:17.401
and Commander Tomi will command
the Eastern Dawn Brigade,

18:17.484 --> 18:19.948
each as a separate unit.

18:20.031 --> 18:23.079
This way, you can receive supplies
from the Black Knights

18:23.162 --> 18:25.333
while ensuring the survival
of your organizations.

18:25.835 --> 18:27.755
Not a bad deal, don't you think?

18:28.089 --> 18:29.091
How about it?

18:30.553 --> 18:32.139
We'll consider it.

18:41.031 --> 18:43.202
Did you let the terrorists escape?

18:43.620 --> 18:45.457
[Divock] Yes, as planned.

18:45.958 --> 18:48.337
Very well. Do as you please.

18:49.298 --> 18:53.347
I swear to you, Lord Norland,
that the fruits of this battle

18:53.849 --> 18:55.435
will be most satisfying.

19:06.958 --> 19:08.252
-[comms beeping]
-[gasps softly]

19:09.839 --> 19:11.593
What is it at this hour?

19:11.676 --> 19:13.471
[woman over comms]
<i>A message from Lord Norland.</i>

19:19.191 --> 19:20.360
[gasps]

19:20.778 --> 19:22.280
[Rozé] Look at that...

19:22.657 --> 19:24.577
Her results aren't the greatest,

19:24.661 --> 19:27.917
but a change of equipment and tactics
could boost her strength exponentially.

19:28.251 --> 19:30.255
She might just surprise us all.

19:30.881 --> 19:31.883
[Kuroto] Rozé.

19:32.718 --> 19:37.269
We've received a response. They have
officially agreed to join the alliance.

19:37.352 --> 19:38.354
Come down.

19:38.437 --> 19:39.439
Got it.

19:41.193 --> 19:43.197
We look forward to working with you.

19:43.699 --> 19:44.867
Likewise.

19:47.915 --> 19:51.297
If I become the ace pilot,
you better make sure to follow my orders.

19:51.380 --> 19:53.009
[Haruka] That's a big "if."

19:53.594 --> 19:54.596
Hang on.

19:55.013 --> 19:57.058
[Oda] The ace unit is all decked out.

19:57.267 --> 20:00.148
So you've noticed!

20:00.231 --> 20:01.400
This Knightmare--

20:01.483 --> 20:04.281
[Rozé] Has been modified for close combat.

20:04.532 --> 20:06.578
I put in a request to General Kuroto.

20:07.287 --> 20:08.289
Haruka.

20:09.626 --> 20:11.504
You'll be piloting the Keisetsu.

20:11.588 --> 20:12.590
Huh?

20:13.257 --> 20:16.347
I've carefully reviewed
your combat record and data.

20:16.640 --> 20:19.979
[Rozé] <i>Your calm judgment and instinct
for swift attacks are impressive.</i>

20:20.063 --> 20:24.572
<i>While not on the same level as Ash,
you're remarkable in every aspect.</i>

20:25.406 --> 20:29.456
It seems that the Akatsuki wasn't able
to fully accommodate your capabilities.

20:29.958 --> 20:33.966
The Keisetsu has been customized
to be easier for you to operate, Haruka.

20:34.049 --> 20:37.263
Well, I'll give it to you this time.

20:37.347 --> 20:38.934
You can cry if you want.

20:39.017 --> 20:40.478
[Rozé] She's all yours.

20:43.401 --> 20:47.075
[Rozé] With that, not even the Einberg
stand a chance against you.

20:47.868 --> 20:51.458
Haruka, you're the ace pilot
of the Seven Shining Stars.

20:54.549 --> 20:56.427
Leave it to me!

20:59.517 --> 21:02.063
-[Hinagata] What the hell?!
-What is it?

21:02.147 --> 21:04.484
They just announced on the news
that Neo-Britannia

21:04.569 --> 21:07.407
is going to exterminate the Japanese
in the Sapporo Ghetto...

21:07.490 --> 21:08.492
[Rozé] What?!

21:10.079 --> 21:12.417
<i>There have long been reports</i>

21:12.500 --> 21:16.133
<i>of numerous terrorists
hiding in the Sapporo Ghetto.</i>

21:16.216 --> 21:17.678
That's a lie!

21:17.762 --> 21:19.264
We're in Hakodate!

21:19.347 --> 21:22.521
We will use F.L.E.I.J.A.

21:22.605 --> 21:25.527
to completely obliterate
the Sapporo Ghetto.

21:26.403 --> 21:28.992
<i>All transportation networks
will be sealed off by the military.</i>

21:29.075 --> 21:32.499
<i>Britannians in the vicinity
are ordered to evacuate immediately.</i>

21:32.958 --> 21:34.796
No Elevens will be permitted to escape!

21:35.379 --> 21:37.885
<i>The operation will commence in 24 hours.</i>

21:39.471 --> 21:40.808
[Shota] 24 hours?

21:40.891 --> 21:42.102
[Oda] What're we gonna do?!

21:45.066 --> 21:46.151
SKY FORTRESS DAMOCLES

21:46.235 --> 21:47.613
[man] <i>Activating Floating System.</i>

21:47.738 --> 21:49.157
-[alarm beeping]
<i>-Releasing lock.</i>

21:50.118 --> 21:51.161
<i>Opening gate.</i>

21:52.288 --> 21:53.708
<i>Launch preparation complete.</i>

21:54.877 --> 21:57.090
Launch the Damocles!

21:57.173 --> 21:59.846
[rumbling]

22:14.959 --> 22:17.422
Are we going to just abandon
the Sapporo Ghetto?!

22:17.756 --> 22:20.846
What're we supposed to do?
Take on the Damocles?!

22:20.929 --> 22:22.850
-[Rozé] We have no choice but to!
-[both gasp]

22:23.058 --> 22:25.062
To defeat Neo-Britannia,

22:25.146 --> 22:27.776
we would've had to
take down the Damocles sooner or later.

22:27.860 --> 22:29.864
The timing has just moved up.

22:30.616 --> 22:33.454
We have the new Eliminator on our side.

22:34.080 --> 22:35.207
The Damocles...

22:37.128 --> 22:39.007
<i>is coming down!</i>

22:40.468 --> 22:42.472
[♪ closing theme music playing]

24:07.893 --> 24:09.897
Translated by Kenji Mouri
